>Ecological correlations and the behavior of individuals</article-title><source>Am Sociol Rev</source><year>1950</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>357</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2087176</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freedman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ecological inference and the ecological fallacy</article-title><source>Prepared for the International Encyclopaedia of the Social and Behavioral Sciences Technical Report No 549</source><year>1999</year><fpage>7</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>AgroSalud: Maps Gallery</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.agrosalud.org/descargas/Galeria_Final/Guatemala/indicadores_nutricionales/antropometirco_riesgo_deficiencia_nutricional.gif"/></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wirth</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Macias</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilde</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Friedman</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mapping hunger: a report on mapping malnutrition prevalence in the Dominican Republic, Ecuador, and Panama</article-title><source>Working Paper in Food Policy and Applied Nutrition</source><year>2007</year><volume>34</volume><publisher-name>Medford MA: Friedman School of Nutrition Science and Policy, Tufts University</publisher-name><fpage>32</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wirth</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Macias</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilde</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mapping hunger in Panama: a report on mapping malnutrition prevalence</article-title><source>Working Paper in Food Policy and Applied Nutrition</source><year>2007</year><volume>35</volume><publisher-name>Medford MA: Friedman School of Nutrition Science and Policy, Tufts University</publisher-name><fpage>27</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Macias</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilde</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Atlas of hunger and malnutrition in the Dominican Republic</article-title><source>Working Paper in Food Policy and Applied Nutrition</source><year>2007</year><volume>36</volume><publisher-name>Medford MA: Friedman School of Nutrition Science and Policy, Tufts University</publisher-name><fpage>32</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wirth</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Macias</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilde</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mapping hunger in Ecuador: a report on mapping malnutrition prevalence</article-title><source>Working Paper in Food Policy and Applied Nutrition</source><year>2007</year><volume>37</volume><publisher-name>Medford MA: Friedman School of Nutrition Science and Policy, Tufts University</publisher-name><fpage>37</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><source>Micro-level estimation of child malnutrition indicators and its application in Cambodia</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Washington, D.C: World Bank Policy Research Working</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics</collab></person-group><source>Local Estimation of Poverty and Malnutrition in Bangladesh</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>In collaboration with UN World Food Programme</publisher-name><fpage>43</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>INEC (Instituto Nacional de Estad&#x000ed;sticas y Censos)</collab></person-group><source>Encuesta Nicarag&#x000fc;ense de Demograf&#x000ed;a y Salud (ENDESA) 2001 Informe B&#x000e1;sico</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Managua: INEC</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>